Bruce <solomon@gehennom.net> writes:

> Far from it.  Most insta-deaths are the results of stupid mistakes.

You people are just deluding yourselves.  Sure, there are insta-death
scenarios that are your own damn fault, but the ones where your
3rd-level character goes downstairs into a dark room and gets "The bolt
of fire hits!  You die . . . " are bloody well not stupid mistakes you
can avoid.  And there are all too many situations like that.  If this
game was truly meant to allow skill to consistently win out over luck,
then it would never do things like give goblins wands of death on
dungeon level 2.

As far as I'm concerned one of the most subtly evil aspects of NetHack
is the way it keeps you thinking that if you had just done this, or
that, or the other thing you would have saved yourself, but most of the
time you would have just died a little later, and no amount of
cleverness then or any different choice any time before that could have
saved you.

